  "summary": "@payloadcms/storage-vercel-blob has access control bypass of uploads in Vercel Storage adapter",
  "details": "### Impact\nIn affected configurations, client upload access does not consistently align with the associated collection’s access configuration.\n\nYou are affected if:\n- You use client uploads with `@payloadcms/storage-vercel-blob`.\n- Authenticated users can access the client-upload route.\n\nApplications that do not enable client uploads are not affected.\n\n### Patches\nClient uploads now require authentication and the appropriate collection-level access before upload access is granted.\n\nUsers should upgrade Payload packages to `>= 3.90.0` or `>= 4.0.0-canary.34`.\n\n### Workarounds\nUpgrading to a patched version is recommended. Until you can upgrade, disable client uploads or configure the upload route’s access control to enforce the associated collection’s permissions.",
